hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"204","From Muhammad bin Bashar, from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, from Israel, from Mansour, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: You consider the verses a punishment, but we used to consider them a blessing during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We used to eat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. While we were listening to the glorification of food, he said: “And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a vessel, and he put his hand in it and made the water spring.” From between his fingers,” so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Live to the blessed purification, and the blessing from God,” until we all performed ablution."
